---
import EnterpriseDetail from '../../components/enterprise/EnterpriseDetail.astro';
import { agentIntegrations } from '../../data/integrations';
---

<EnterpriseDetail
  slug="agent-agnostic"
  seoTitle="Agent Choice | SAM Enterprise"
  seoDescription={`Run ${agentIntegrations.map((a) => a.shortName ?? a.name).join(', ')} on one self-hosted platform. Each user brings their own keys or subscriptions; profiles pick the agent per task.`}
  title="Use the agents your teams already like"
  subtitle="SAM is not tied to one agent or model vendor. Each chat or task runs the agent its profile names, so different teams can make different choices on the same installation."
>
  <h2>Supported agents</h2>
  <ul>
    {agentIntegrations.map((agent) => (
      <li><a href={`/integrations/${agent.slug}/`}>{agent.name}</a>: {agent.tagline}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>
    The <a href="/integrations/#ai-agents">integrations page</a> compares how each one signs in.
  </p>

  <h2>Accounts and keys</h2>
  <p>
    Each user connects their own API keys or subscriptions, and can connect several for one agent, such as a work
    subscription and a client's API key, then pin each to the projects or profiles that should use it. Projects can
    also share a credential so members do not each need one.
  </p>
  <p>
    Claude Code and Codex can also point at a compatible endpoint, such as a gateway your company already runs,
    or use the installation's own AI proxy if an administrator enables it. SAM does not integrate directly with
    Amazon Bedrock, Google Vertex AI or Azure OpenAI.
  </p>

  <h2>Profiles</h2>
  <p>
    A profile names an agent, model and settings. Rolling out a new agent or model to a team means adding or
    editing a profile, and every chat, task or trigger that uses it picks up the change.
  </p>

  <h2>If you change your mind</h2>
  <p>
    Switching agents is a profile change. Your projects, chat history, triggers and machines stay where they are.
    Because SAM itself is open source, you can also keep running it whatever happens to the project.
  </p>
</EnterpriseDetail>
